<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/03e1f1c7aadf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chinese facial recognition system mistakes a face on a bus for a jaywalker" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "517" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0431cb50e0d8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[513] Famous businesswoman Dong Mingzhu, who chairs China’s largest air conditioner manufacturing company, was misidentified as a jaywalker at an intersection in Ningbo in eastern China, calling into question the technology’s accuracy and liveness detection capabilities." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ed601c2b005> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[513] Famous businesswoman Dong Mingzhu, who chairs China’s largest air conditioner manufacturing company, was misidentified as a jaywalker at an intersection in Ningbo in eastern China, calling into question the technology’s accuracy and liveness detection capabilities." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1dd42849817c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Using sophisticated AI algorithms, Chinese technology companies and other major businesses have adopted facial recognition systems in retail, travel and financial services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "519" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e9cd656189a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It also said the facial recognition system will be upgraded to avoid such incidents in future." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "512" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1f1104dce13b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The woman in question was Dong Mingzhu, Chairwoman of China’s biggest maker of air conditioners, Gree Electric Appliances." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "506" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/24a4f2202c8d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Facial recognition catches China’s air con queen Dong Mingzhu jaywalking, but turns out to be ..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "508" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/250a3b4ffc7c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[511] China has been using gait recognition as well as face recognition to automate the ticketing of jaywalkers, much like cameras are used in the USA to ticket people who run red lights." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/310f2b7e4d6d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Officials have also talked to WeChat and Weibo about potentially fining offenders via text messages." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "517" .

